## MLOps

One of the most important things I learned from this course was the fundamental concept of **MLOps**.

MLOps extends beyond simply building and deploying an ML model. It provides a systematic and repeatable approach to developing, deploying, monitoring and improving machine learning systems.

Instead of:

Build → Deploy → Done

MLOps is more like:

Develop → Train → Evaluate → Deploy → Monitor → Improve/Retrain → Redeploy

This showed me that machine learning in the real world requires continuous management and improvement.

## My Key Takeaway

The biggest lesson I took from this course is that building a good ML model is not simply about achieving a high score on a dataset.

A successful ML solution should:

1. Solve the intended business problem.
2. Use appropriate data and features.
3. Generalize well to unseen data.
4. Be evaluated using metrics that reflect the actual objective.
5. Be deployed appropriately.
6. Be monitored and continuously improved.

This course helped me move from understanding the **ML process** to understanding more about how ML solutions can actually be **developed, evaluated, deployed and maintained in production**.

